  "notes": "The retro-and-Latin pole. The modelled kit is the first of her three and the entry names it first: \"a dry retro-soul kit with a damped snare on 2&4, tambourine and no hat carpet\", which is why `halfTime` is false, the hat carpet is nearly off and the tambourine is a constant; the dembow and trap kits are documented in the entry and recorded here rather than authored as `modes`, since the volume gives them no separate harmony. ⛔ **`bass808` is null** on the entry's own default: \"played electric bass with flatwounds and bossa-style root-fifth motion on the retro material\" — so the bass is a real part with `P5` at the head of its passing tones, which is what \"root-fifth motion\" means. Her home keys are authored as stated (F♯ minor and F minor \"to an unusual degree\", with A♭ and D♭ major for the retro material). Harmony is \"60s-soul/bossa-derived — maj7/m7 with real cadences and chromatic passing chords\", so the seventh share is the highest in this batch and `susOrDimProb` carries the chromatic approach. The melody is \"light, high, breathy soprano with a deliberately childlike timbre… low-to-moderate note-density, small intervals\", i.e. a near-stepwise interval spread. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are the swing amount, every drum number and the bassline figures; the entry marks drum detail as idiom inference. ⚠ `confidence` is medium — the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ **`drums.kick.lockTo808` removed (2026-08-17, 808 gate).** This kit has no 808 — `bass808` is `null` here or in the parent it inherits — and `lockTo808` is the one parameter that says *how much of the kick the 808 follows*, so in this file it described a pairing that does not exist: `generators::drums::bass808` returns on `block.is_none()` before the value is ever read, which makes it provably dead here. Where it was NOT dead was in the artists and producers who extend this kit and author an 808 of their own: they inherited the zero, `kicks.iter().filter(|_| rng.random_bool(0.0))` kept nothing, and their sub lane was silent at every seed — `bass808::every_shipped_model_with_an_808_produces_a_playable_line` reported \"no 808 at all\" for 35 of them. Removing it restores the engine's documented default of 1.0 for exactly those children and changes nothing here. ⚠ No researched claim moved: this kit's own statement about the 808 is the `bass808: null` beside it, and that is untouched.",
